From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/esp32: add opt-in external ESP-NOW peer bridge

Connect two independent emulated WiFi controllers over an explicit IPv4
loopback UDP fixture. Guest TX still traverses the normal controller DMA
path, and peer delivery is injected through the peer controller's normal RX
DMA path.

The bridge forwards management action frames only. It is default-off, rejects
invalid or unpaired ports and cannot be combined with the same-guest loopback
fixture. Classic ESP32 sessions bind controller and RX-filter identity to the
same session-derived station MAC. This proves an unencrypted external-guest
action-frame exchange. It does not model PMK/LMK encryption, CCMP, loss/retry,
RF, antenna or timing.

Signed-off-by: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
---
 3 files changed, 266 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

